From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:40:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: G-PHY: don't decode OFDM frames as HT

b43_rx() reads both bits of B43_RX_PHYST0_FTYPE to tell 802.11n frames
apart. A G-PHY sets bit 1 for its OFDM frames as well, so each OFDM
frame was decoded as HT, with rate_idx 108 (0x6c, the first PLCP byte),
and mac80211 dropped it with a warning:

  Rate marked as an HT rate but passed status->rate_idx is not an MCS
  index [0-76]: 108 (0x6c)

On an ASUS WL-320gE (BCM5352, G-PHY rev 7, radio 2050 rev 2) as an AP,
69% of pings were lost at idle and no TCP connection came up, with
firmware 784.2 and 666.2 alike.

Only N-PHY and HT-PHY tell 802.11n frames apart. On any other PHY, read
the OFDM bit only, as before.

Signed-off-by: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
@@ -1155,6 +1155,7 @@ void b43_rx(struct b43_wldev *dev, struc
 	const struct b43_rxhdr_fw4 *rxhdr = _rxhdr;
 	__le16 fctl;
 	u16 phystat0, phystat3;
+	u16 ftype;
 	u16 chanstat, mactime;
 	u32 macstat;
 	u16 chanid;
@@ -1273,7 +1274,12 @@ void b43_rx(struct b43_wldev *dev, struc
 		}
 	}
 
-	switch (phystat0 & B43_RX_PHYST0_FTYPE) {
+	ftype = phystat0 & B43_RX_PHYST0_FTYPE;
+	/* Only N-PHY and HT-PHY tell 802.11n frames apart; a G-PHY also sets
+	 * bit 1 for OFDM frames, which would then be decoded as HT */
+	if (dev->phy.type != B43_PHYTYPE_N && dev->phy.type != B43_PHYTYPE_HT)
+		ftype &= B43_RX_PHYST0_OFDM;
+	switch (ftype) {
 	case B43_RX_PHYST0_PRE_N:
 	case B43_RX_PHYST0_STD_N:
 		/*
